      "description": "Provide detailed context-sensitive help material for all UI actions",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "The solution should provide detailed context-sensitive help material for all the possible actions and scenarios on all user interfaces in the application."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_002",
      "description": "Provide interface for logging and tracking defects/enhancements",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_TRACK_DEFECT", "FUN_TRACK_ENHANCEMENT"],
      "source_text": "The solution should provide an interface for the user to log any defects or enhancement requests on the application and track thereafter."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_003",
      "description": "Send alerts to users when actions are taken on alerts",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEND_ALERT"],
      "source_text": "The solution should send alerts (e.g., email, SMS) to the user if the user chooses to whenever any action has been taken on the alert."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_004",
      "description": "Maintain unalterable audit trail for critical entities",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_REGISTER_CASE", "FUN_UPDATE_CASE", "FUN_DELETE_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must keep an unalterable audit trail capable of automatically capturing and storing information about:The word 'unalterable' is to mean that the audit trail data cannot be modified in any way or deleted by any user; it may be subject to re-department and copying to removable media if required, so long as its contents remain unchanged."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_005",
      "description": "Automatically track events and store audit trail information",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_REGISTER_CASE", "FUN_UPDATE_CASE", "FUN_DELETE_CASE"],
      "source_text": "Once the audit trail functionality has been activated, the System must track events without manual intervention, and store in the audit trail information about them."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_006",
      "description": "Maintain audit trail for at least the life of the related case",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_REGISTER_CASE", "FUN_UPDATE_CASE", "FUN_DELETE_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must maintain the audit trail for as long as required, which will be at least for the life of the case to which it refers."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_007",
      "description": "Ensure audit trail data is available for inspection on request",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_EXPORT_AUDIT_TRAIL"],
      "source_text": "The System must ensure that audit trail data is available for inspection on request, so that a specific event can be identified and all related data made accessible, and that this can be achieved by authorised external personnel who have little or no familiarity with the system."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_008",
      "description": "Export audit trails for specified cases",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_EXPORT_AUDIT_TRAIL"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to export audit trails for specified cases (without affecting the audit trail stored by the System). This functionality can be used by external auditors who wish to examine or analyse system activity."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_009",
      "description": "Capture and store access control violations",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_ACCESS"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to capture and store violations (i.e. A user's attempts to access a case to which he is denied access), and (where violations can validly be attempted) attempted violations, of access control mechanisms."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_010",
      "description": "Allow limiting case access to specified users/groups",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_ACCESS"],
      "source_text": "The System must allow the user to limit access to cases to specified users or user groups."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_011",
      "description": "Provide role-based control for system functionality",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_ACCESS"],
      "source_text": "The system should provide for role-based control for the functionality within the system"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_012",
      "description": "Allow users to be members of multiple groups",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_ACCESS"],
      "source_text": "The System must allow a user to be a member of more than one group."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_013",
      "description": "Only admin-users can set up user profiles and allocate users to groups",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_USER"],
      "source_text": "The System must allow only admin-users to set up user profiles and allocate users to groups."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_014",
      "description": "Only super-user can change security attributes",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_MANAGE_USER"],
      "source_text": "The System must allow changes to security attributes for groups or users (such as access rights, security level, privileges, password allocation and management) to be made only by super-user."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_015",
      "description": "Provide configurable responses for unauthorized case access attempts",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_VIEW_CASE", "FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "If a user requests access to, or searches for, a case which he does not have the right to access, the System must provide one of the following responses (selectable at configuration time):These options are presented in order of increasing security. Note that the requirement in the third option (i.e. the most stringent) implies that the System must not include such cases in any count of search results; this level of security is normally appropriate for cases dealing with matters such as national security."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_016",
      "description": "Never include unauthorized records in search results",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "If a user performs a quick or advanced search, the System must never include in the search result list any record which the user does not have the right to access."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_017",
      "description": "Log unauthorized case access attempts to audit trail",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_VIEW_CASE", "FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "If the System allows users to make unauthorised attempts to access cases, it must log these in the audit trail."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_018",
      "description": "All error messages must be meaningful",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "All error messages produced by the System must be meaningful, so that they can be appropriately acted upon by the users who are likely to see them. Ideally, each error message will be accompanied by explanatory text and an indication of the action(s) which the user can take in response to the error."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_019",
      "description": "Employ consistent UI rules for common look and feel",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "The System must employ a single set of user interface rules, or a small number of sets to provide a familiar and common look and feel for the application."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_020",
      "description": "Display multiple entities simultaneously",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_VIEW_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to display several entities (cases, suspects) simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_021",
      "description": "Make interfaces customizable and save configurations in user profile",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "The interfaces must be made customizable or user-configurable to the extent possible. (e.g., the displayed columns in the table, move, resize, modify the appearance). Such configurations must be saved in the user profile."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_022",
      "description": "Ensure UI is suitable for users with special needs",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "The System user interface must be suitable for users with special needs; that is, compatible with specialist software that may be used and with appropriate interface guidelines"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_023",
      "description": "Perform simple search within 5-8 seconds, advanced search within 10-15 seconds",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to perform a simple search within 5-8 seconds and a advanced search (multiple search criteria) within 10-15 seconds regardless of the storage capacity or number of cases in the system. In this context, performing a search means returning a result list. It does not include retrieving the records themselves."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_024",
      "description": "Retrieve and display recently accessed cases within 5-8 seconds",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_VIEW_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to retrieve and display within 5-8 seconds the case which has been accessed within the previous 2 months, regardless of storage capacity or number of cases in the system. This requirement is intended to allow for rapid retrieval of frequently-used cases, on the understanding that frequency of use is typically correlated with recent use."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_025",
      "description": "Retrieve and display infrequently accessed cases within 20 seconds",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_VIEW_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The System must be able to retrieve and display within 20 seconds the case which has not been accessed within the previous 2 months, regardless of storage capacity or number of cases in the system. This requirement is intended to allow for cases where cases used infrequently are stored on slower media than more active records."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_026",
      "description": "System must be scalable for different police station sizes",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "The System be scaleable and must not have any features which would preclude use in small or large police stations, with varying numbers of cases handled."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_027",
      "description": "Support multilingual interface",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "The system should support multilingual interface"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_028",
      "description": "Design to prevent operational data loss during failures",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "The system should be designed in manner that operational data is not lost in case of any failure of equipment or communication network."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_029",
      "description": "Use HTTPS as communication protocol",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "The system should use HTTPS as the communication protocol, i.e., HTTP over an encrypted secure socket layer (SSL))"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_030",
      "description": "Support selective encryption of stored data",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_ENCRYPT_DATA"],
      "source_text": "The system should support selective encryption of the stored data"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_031",
      "description": "Ensure secure data transmission using SSL and 2-way digital signatures",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_ENCRYPT_DATA"],
      "source_text": "The system should ensure secure transmission of data over the network and utilize SSL and 2-way digital signatures"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_032",
      "description": "Prevent cross-site scripting",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "Prevent cross-site scripting"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_033",
      "description": "Prevent SQL injection",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "Prevent SQL Injection"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_034",
      "description": "No hard deletes, only soft tagging for deletion",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_DELETE_CASE"],
      "source_text": "Do not allow hard delete and perform only soft tagging the row for deletion"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_035",
      "description": "Use cache for storing frequent data",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "Use of cache for storing frequent data"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_036",
      "description": "Fetch search results in batches of 10 or 20",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The search results should be fetched from the database in batches of 10 or 20 maximum as configured within the application"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_037",
      "description": "Fetch only fields needed for display in search",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "The search should fetch only the fields that need to be displayed to the user. Only when the user clicks on a particular record to view its further details should a query be fired to fetch the additional details for this particular record only"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_038",
      "description": "Apply database indexes on key search columns",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_SEARCH_CASE"],
      "source_text": "Database Indexes should be applied on the key columns used for searching"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_039",
      "description": "UI should comply with ISO 9241 standard",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "The user interfaces of the system should comply with Standard ISO 9241."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_040",
      "description": "Application logo available on all pages as home link",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "The application logo to be available on all pages as a link to the home page."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_041",
      "description": "Provide text equivalents for non-text media objects",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "All non-text media objects, such as graphical images or video, should be provided with alternative equivalent textual descriptions and/or with equivalent text-based functionality."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_042",
      "description": "Design navigation to help users understand location and options",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Navigation should be designed to help users understand where they are, where they have been and where they can go next. General guidance on achieving self-descriptiveness is given in ISO 9241-110."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_043",
      "description": "Show users their location in navigation structure",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Each presentation segment (page or window) should provide the user with a clear and sufficient indication of where he or she is in the navigation structure and of the current segment position with respect to the overall structure."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_044",
      "description": "Offer alternative access paths for navigation",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Alternative access paths for navigating to a specific unit of content should be offered to support different navigation strategies."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_045",
      "description": "Minimize navigation steps needed to reach content",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "The number of navigation steps needed to reach a certain piece of content should be minimized as long as different mental models, navigation strategies and tasks of the user are taken into account."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_046",
      "description": "Avoid splash screens unless they provide useful content",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Splash screens should be avoided unless they provide useful content or feedback about the application state to the user. If a splash screen is used, a navigation option to skip it should be offered."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_047",
      "description": "Avoid opening unnecessary windows",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Additional windows such as new browser windows or pop-up windows should only be opened if this supports the user's task. Opening new windows can distract, confuse or impede users for a variety of reasons. They can superimpose the primary window, hiding relevant information. They could make it cognitively more difficult to understand the navigation structure with negative effects on both usability and accessibility. They also require additional user actions for closing unwanted windows."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_048",
      "description": "Minimize vertical scrolling, avoid horizontal scrolling",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Vertical scrolling should be minimized. This may be done by placing important information at the top and providing links to information that is further down the page. Horizontal scrolling should be avoided wherever possible."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_049",
      "description": "Design UI for input device independence",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "User interfaces should be designed to allow activation of controls by a variety of input devices. The ability to choose between different input devices for activating controls such as links, fields and buttons is important both for users who prefer a certain input mode, mobile users and users with disabilities. In general, device independence can be achieved if the functionality is operable via a keyboard."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_050",
      "description": "Design UI to be robust against technology changes",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Making user interfaces robust: User interfaces should be designed to be as robust as possible in the face of changing technology. This encompasses being able to present content containing newer technologies by older user agents as well as designing content to be usable with future technologies."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_051",
      "description": "Ensure acceptable page opening/download times",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Application pages should be designed and implemented so that there are acceptable opening times and download times for the expected range of technical contexts of use (e.g. bandwidth between the application and the user). This is particularly important for frequently accessed pages or pages that are important for user navigation and exploration, such as the home page."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_052",
      "description": "Minimize potential user errors and recovery effort",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "Minimizing user errors: Potential user errors as well as the effort needed to recover from errors should be minimized."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_053",
      "description": "Provide clear error messages with resolution actions",
      "related_functions": [],
      "source_text": "Providing clear error messages: The content of error messages shown on the pages or special error pages should clearly state the reason why the error occurred and, if possible, actions the user can take to resolve the error. Users expect error messages to be in the same language as the user interface."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_054",
      "description": "Allow users to resize text",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Making text resizable by the user: Text should be able to be resized by the user, using functions provided by the user agent or other appropriate means i.e. see ISO 9241-171."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_055",
      "description": "Ensure text quality does not impede readability",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Text quality: The quality of textual content with respect to spelling and grammar should be sufficient so as not to impede readability."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_056",
      "description": "Support fast text skimming with clear links and lists",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Supporting text skimming: Fast skimming of text should be supported by the provision of clear links, bulleted lists, highlighted keywords, logical headings, and short phrases and sentences."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_057",
      "description": "Clearly distinguish within-page links from other links",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Distinguishable within-page links: Within-page links should be clearly distinguishable from other links that lead to a different page. EX. Within-page links are shown with dashed rather than solid underlines"
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_058",
      "description": "Avoid link overload that impedes text readability",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Avoiding link overload: Text pages containing large proportions of links should be formatted so that the presence of links does not impede the readability of the text."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_059",
      "description": "Use familiar terminology for navigation links",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Using familiar terminology for navigation links: Navigation links — particularly links representing the main navigation structure — should be labelled with terms that are familiar to the user, based on his/her general knowledge, prior experience in the application domain or experience of using other systems."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_060",
      "description": "Use descriptive link labels indicating target/purpose",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Using descriptive link labels: The target or purpose of a link should be directly indicated by its label, avoiding generic labels such as 'go' or 'click here' except where the purpose of the link is clear from its context on the page or the labels have commonly understood semantics in the particular application domain. Using appropriate terminology specific to the user's tasks and information needs is important for making the content easy to understand."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_061",
      "description": "Clearly mark links that open new windows",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Marking links opening new windows: Links that open new browser windows or pop-up windows should be clearly marked."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_062",
      "description": "Clearly distinguish navigation links from action controls",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Distinguishing navigation links from controls: Navigation links should be clearly distinguishable from controls activating some action. Typical action types in user interfaces include manipulating application data, performing searches, communication actions, such as opening a new e-mail window or starting a chat function, and presentation-related actions, such as sorting a list of search results."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_063",
      "description": "Provide printable versions for long documents",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_GENERATE_REPORT"],
      "source_text": "Providing printable document versions: If a document is either too long, dispersed over several pages or in a specific layout that is not suitable for online reading, a printer-friendly version of the document should be provided that prints the content in a form acceptable to the user (e.g. in the expected layout, paper format, or orientation)."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_064",
      "description": "Use white space carefully to not impair visual skimming",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Use of 'white space': 'White space' on a page i.e. space filled only with the background color should be used in such a way that it does not impair the visual skimming of the page. While white space is an important means of visually organizing the different content elements on a page, if the distance between the blocks of information displayed becomes too large, rapid skimming of the page can be impeded."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_065",
      "description": "Select appropriate page lengths based on purpose",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Selecting appropriate page lengths The length of a page should be selected so as to support the primary purpose and use of the page. Short pages are generally more appropriate for homepages, navigation pages, or overview pages that need to be read quickly. Longer pages can be more appropriate when users want to read the content without interruptions or when the page needs to match a paper counterpart."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_066",
      "description": "Use color carefully, not as sole information means",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Using colour: Colour should be used with care, taking into account human capabilities and restrictions in perceiving colour, and not as the only means of conveying information. Color should never be the only means of coding. Some users may have difficulties in perceiving certain colors or color combinations (color-blindness)."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_067",
      "description": "Use frames carefully with alternatives",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Using frames with care: If frames are used, care should be taken to avoid possible problems, for example, those involving the use of the back button, bookmarking of pages, or scrolling of information. When frames are used, it is important to title each frame, and to describe its purpose and how frames relate to one another other. Providing alternatives to frame-based presentation: If frames are used, an alternative way of presenting relevant information without frames should be provided. Providing alternative text-only pages: When style sheets and/or frames are turned off it should be possible for the user to read and understand the page; alternatively, the user should be provided with an equivalent alternative text-only page."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_068",
      "description": "Use consistent layout schemes across pages",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Consistent page layout: Pages should be designed using consistent layout schemes, supporting the user in finding similar information at the same position on different pages. Overall layout schemes apply to all pages and are preferable when all pages have a similar structure. Frequently, however, different pages have different purposes and types of content. In such cases, pages can usually be grouped in different categories, using one layout scheme for each category consistently."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_069",
      "description": "Place title information consistently across pages",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Placing title information consistently: Page titles should be placed in a consistent location on the different pages."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_070",
      "description": "Consider principles of human perception in UI design",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Observing principles of human perception When designing application pages, the general principles of human perception should be taken into account. The International Standards mentioned below shall be consulted for guidance. Practical guidelines for presenting information to the user are to be found in ISO 9241-12. Guidance on selecting and using different forms of interaction techniques is to be found in ISO 9241-14 to ISO 9241-17. ISO 9241-14 gives guidance about menus, ISO 9241-15 about command dialogues, ISO 9241-16 about direct manipulation and ISO 9241-17 about forms. In addition, when designing multimedia information presentations, the design principles and recommendations described in ISO 14915-1 to ISO 14915-3 should be taken into account. Appropriate content presentation also plays a key role in accessibility."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_071",
      "description": "Include link to home/landmark page on each page",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Linking back to the home page or landmark pages: Each page should contain a link leading to the home page of the application or to a landmark page that is easy to recognize for the user."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_072",
      "description": "Provide site map showing application structure",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Providing a site map: A separate navigation overview such as a site map should be provided for application showing the structure of the site in an overview form."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_073",
      "description": "Maintain consistency between navigation components and content",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Consistency between navigation components and content: If navigation components (or overviews) are shown in conjunction with associated content, consistency between the navigation component and the content shown should be maintained by indicating in the navigation component (e.g. highlighting) the topic currently visible in the content area."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_074",
      "description": "Place navigation components consistently",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_NAVIGATE"],
      "source_text": "Placing navigation components consistently: Navigation components should be placed consistently on the pages or in the framesets in the pages of the application."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_075",
      "description": "Make individualization/adaptation evident to users",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Making individualization and adaptation evident: It should be made evident to the user when individualization and/or adaptation are used."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_076",
      "description": "Make current user profile evident when used",
      "related_functions": ["FUN_CUSTOMIZE_UI"],
      "source_text": "Making user profiles evident: If predefined user profiles or user-specified profiles are used for individualizing or adapting content, the profile currently used should be made evident. If profiles are used, it is important to provide users with information about this concept and its implications."
    },
    {
      "constraintRef": "C_RULE_077",
      "description": "Allow users to see, modify and delete their profiles",
